	"_note": "DEMONSTRATION FIXTURE, and the only one in this directory that is not adversarial. The three critic_* studies beside it exist to break the kit; this one exists to answer the opposite question - CAN the kit make a deckhouse a person would accept? Same 28 x 10 m hull as critic_ferry, and every difference from it is data: the house is pulled in to x 2.0..8.0 so there are 2.0 m SIDE DECKS a 1.8 m figure walks down (the ferry roofs 90% of the beam); the height is STEPPED 2.0 -> 3.0 -> 5.5 m across three tiers instead of one constant 2.5 m slab; the window band CHANGES along the length - a 1.5 m saloon ribbon of four lights forward, a higher-silled 1.0 m galley band of two aft on starboard, punched scuttles in the low casing, and a solid panel where the door goes on port; and there are TWO DOORS, one into the house off the port side deck and one into the wheelhouse off the boat deck. Nothing here is a new piece and nothing is a new parameter - 39 placements of the same six pieces, at four wall heights and three tier levels.",
